.bmad-loop/cache/
# .bmad-loop/policy.toml — DELIBERATELY VERSION-CONTROLLED (2026-08-05).
# bmad-loop's init gitignores this file by default, treating it as machine-local
# config. Here it is the opposite: it declares WHICH MODEL execution runs on
# ([adapter] model) and WHETHER runs are isolated ([scm] isolation). Ignored, a
# reinstall or a second machine silently reverts both to the shipped defaults —
# full Opus sessions, writing into the shared checkout. Both are decisions with
# a cost and a blast radius, so they belong in history, not in a local file.
# Each deviation carries its rationale at the point of override, inside the file.
_bmad/render/
